213	 ## The bell: `wss://runlog.scrthq.com/ws?run=<runId>&t=<token>`
214	 
215	 A WebSocket that says when the run moves, so a plugin need not poll hard. It accepts the same token and watches that one run. Each message is JSON:
216	 
217	 ```json
218	 { "t": "changed", "id": "01J…", "seq": 42 }
219	 ```
220	 
221	 `seq` climbs with every move. On a message, fetch the metrics again. The socket carries no state of its own; it only rings.
222	 
223	+The gateway drops a socket that sits ten minutes without a frame in either direction, so a client waiting out a quiet Play step should send a small one now and then to hold the line open:
224	+
225	+| `t` | Does |
226	+| --- | --- |
227	+| `ping` | Sent by a client to keep an idle socket open. Answered `{ "t": "pong" }`, to the sender alone. |
228	+| `pong` | The server's answer to a `ping`. Ignored; nothing reads it. |
229	+
230	 The socket also carries **gestures**: things happening at the table that are not moves, passed straight through and stored nowhere:
231	 
232	 ```json
233	 { "t": "gesture", "id": "01J…", "kind": "rolled", "from": "Mira", "at": "2026-09-07T20:14:03.120Z",
234	   "data": { "dice": [{ "faces": 20, "display": "14", "label": "d20" }], "total": 14, "label": "Kiln Check", "notation": "1d20" } }
235	 ```
236	 
237	 The kinds:
238	 
239	 | `kind` | When | `data` |
